>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_term_postprocessor`

``` hol4
Refute.register_term_postprocessor :
  hol_type -> term_postprocessor -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a display-only model-term transformation.

``` hol4
type term_postprocessor = term -> term
```

The first argument is a HOL type pattern.  Every pattern matching a
model term's actual type participates.  General patterns run before
strictly more specific ones; otherwise older registrations run first.
Re-registering an alpha-equivalent pattern replaces its callback without
changing that position.

Refute snapshots the registry for a model display and applies the
composed transformations bottom-up.  If a callback raises a
non-interrupt exception or changes the term's type, its result is ignored
and composition continues from that callback's input candidate.  Interrupts are
re-raised.  Postprocessing never changes raw model values or
certification.

Registrations are session-local and synchronized with the other model
registries.  `Refute.lookup_term_postprocessor ty` returns the currently
composed callback for `ty`, if any.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.register_frac_type_rat`](#Refute.register_frac_type_rat),
[`Refute.register_frac_type_real`](#Refute.register_frac_type_real),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model reconstruction is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
